course: dictionary
lesson: 12685
title: Diurnal: active in the day
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Diurnal» is a science word that describes animals, and things, that are active during the day. Diurnal animals wake up, feed and move around in daylight, then rest at night. Like most birds, butterflies and humans, they are diurnal.
explain: «Butterflies are diurnal, so you often see them flying on sunny afternoons.» The sentence tells you when butterflies are busy, which is the clue. Diurnal must mean active in the day, because the afternoon is in the day.
explain: Diurnal has a second meaning: happening every day, or during the day. «The diurnal temperature changes» means the temperature goes up and down each day. The opposite of diurnal is nocturnal, which means active at night.
explain: A good check is to swap in the words «active in the day» and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning. If you are not sure, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: Diurnal means active during the day and resting at night.
fact: Like most birds, butterflies and humans, many animals are diurnal.
fact: The opposite of diurnal is nocturnal, which means active at night.
fact: Crepuscular animals are active at dawn and dusk, in between the two.
fact: «Diurnal range» is the difference between the highest and lowest temperature in one day, so it is measured in geography.
exercise: «Butterflies are diurnal, so you usually see them flying in the day.» What does diurnal mean? | Happening only once a year | Active at night | Very loud | *Active during the day
exercise: Which of these is a diurnal animal? | Owl | Bat | Badger | *Robin
exercise: «Owls are nocturnal, not diurnal.» Find and copy the word that is the opposite of diurnal. | *nocturnal | diurnal | owls | not
test: «The diurnal temperature changes» in the desert are large. What does diurnal mean here? | Happening only at night | Lasting for one hour | *Happening every day | Very cold
test: In geography, «diurnal range» means | The average rainfall in a month | The highest temperature of the year | The time the sun sets | *The difference between the highest and lowest temperature in one day
exam: Which description fits a diurnal animal? | *Feeds and moves about in daylight, then rests at night | Lives underground in the dark | Only comes out at dusk | Sleeps all day and hunts at night
